A||||3||loafer87gt||Venom Performance Parts for V6!||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||03-18-2000||12:21 PM||||Hey guys, I was reading through the new Sport Compact Car magazine and found a company called Venom Performance. They make some neat parts for the GM V6. The thing that caught my eye was a really trick looking intake manifold for 90+ Aluminum 3.1's. I know that this has been the big problem with upgrading to the later gen aluminum heads, that the intake doesn't match up with the factory Fiero ones. Shouldn't a guy be able to bolt this new manifold up to the lighter weight aluminum heads? They also have bigger throttle bodies, Fuel rails, fuel injectors, and a performance control module that looks real sweet too. Anyways, I'm rambling on now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Check it out at <A HREF="http://www.venom-performance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.venom-performance.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||03-18-2000||06:52 PM||||Not to burst ANY bubbles or cast shadows and SURELY not to bad mouth any one (Got nailed for that with spark plug wire manufacture when I worked at NOPI if anyone askes... VITEK wires are great...) If you guys, ANYONE really wants to know about VENOM and any of their products. Go to the Engineered Performance web page  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>   e-mail them for the dyno sheets of the 3 Venom SPONCERED local cars. (Black Vemon Civic - progressive throttle control, nitrous controller, and some other shiney magic black box - along with 2 other cars)  That same day, The owner paid the shop to take those pieces off his car and shipped them back to VENOM and took the Sponcership stickers off his car. Thier Injectors are great! Along with the fuel pumps. Thier sheet metal work i'm not familiar with. But I personaly would stay away from their "Magic Boxes" I can tear apart their "Dyno specs" they show on their add for thier Progressive Trhottle control too... If you see the graph... they show percentage of throttle opening, and hp and tq. Who races at part throttle? Do i really need 7% more torque at 10% throttle open and NO load.. NO i'm puttsin' down the off ramp at the throttle position. If you look at the top of the graph they have, the numbers match.. which means NO gain at full throttle. $400 bucks for no gain.. ALL the carb manufactures make basicly the same thing its called a throttle CAM. all it does is trick either the Computer or force the carb to open faster or more at a given accelerator pedal position.. It works on carb cars.. not fuel injected cars.. the computer doesn't understand whats going on and FLAKES! And thier Nitrous controller.. oh man.. well i'll tell ya about that later... but, Good idea and even better concept.. just poor execution also makes ya wonder why they ONLY use thier injectors and fuel pump but use a HAL-Tec to run thier 10sec 1/4 civic and not thie magic box..  huuumm.. they found thier nitch and making a killing more power to em... Sorry for the vent everyone! I'll go get the vemon web address and post it too... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-18-2000||06:58 PM||||Oh nevermind... Loafer already posted it. I'm sure the intake would do just fine no magic in sheet metal. ANd thier intakes have nitrous bosses alredy on then for a fogger kit!!! just use caution when considering their electronics. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||03-19-2000||12:01 PM||||Does anyone know if you could use the aluminum heads from a 3.1 with the Venom intake on our Fiero? Will it match up to our throttle body allright? ||||reg||1
